flag(33,'calculations explanation','The o4 rationale is arithmetically wrong: flipping the first standardized sign changes (-1,1) to (1,1), then applying gain (2,3) and offset (1,-1) gives (3,2), not (1,2). The offered value (1,2) instead results if the first scaled component is omitted. Correct the rationale or the option coherently.')
flag(34,'answerSet explanation distractors','The keyed option overstates the mathematical defect: division by a small but nonzero variance-derived denominator is not undefined. Separate zero-variance division-by-zero from numerical sensitivity or underflow at very small variance. The wrong alternatives about future tokens, vocabulary distributions and forced zero gain/offset should also be replaced by plausible stabilizer mechanisms.')
flag(35,'distractors','The wrong alternatives deny the visible residuals, normalize only after the whole model, or replace normalization with token sampling. Use parallel pre-norm/post-norm placements and distinguish source architecture variation without obvious impossibilities.')
flag(37,'distractors','A vocabulary probability for every training example and one head’s full score matrix do not plausibly describe a single row of X. Use token/feature/sequence/batch orientation alternatives of comparable scope.')
flag(39,'sourceSupport','The key and explanation combine known-input parallelization with causal masking and sequential prefix generation, but only p1494 is cited. Add p1495 for the mask and p1480 for autoregressive extension, with corresponding concept premises.')
flag(47,'distractors','A vocabulary vector of sampled IDs and one scalar shared by all positions are not plausible readings of the vectorized head output. Use alternative matrix shapes/index interpretations while retaining the useful head-index versus token-index confusion.')
flag(50,'distractors','All IDs mapping to the first entry is implausible. Test off-by-one conventions using coherent index/vector pairs instead of unrelated embedding values and collapsed lookups.')
flag(51,'distractors','All three wrong answers restate versions of an absolute one-word-one-token rule, making the sole qualified answer conspicuous. Use distinct plausible tokenizer/sequence-length inferences, preserving the example-specific scope.')
flag(54,'distractors','The wrong choices replace attention with IDs, equate vocabulary size with batch size, or force every full representation identical. Use meaningful contrasts such as token identity, order, contextual interaction and output normalization.')
