flag(57,'distractors','o4 equates the probability vector with token IDs and o1 treats embeddings as probabilities. Prefer parallel alternative matrix relationships, independent learned U, weight sharing without transposition, or bias-only sharing.')
flag(60,'distractors','All wrong alternatives use position IDs alone, an unprocessed first token ID, or a not-yet-existing future state. Compare the last contextual row with other actual contextual rows, their mean, or a specifically labeled shifted input/output row.')
flag(65,'distractors','o2 says p means 80 tokens despite p=0.8. Replace it with a realistic inclusive-versus-strict boundary, individual-probability cutoff or renormalization error.')
flag(69,'distractors','Unknown output prediction without input and hiding every input after the first are poor alternatives. Compare causal, bidirectional, local-window and task/padding-masked attention over a known input.')
